@page "/Tutorials/Spellcasting-Guide"

<div class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 min-h-screen font-sans">

    <!-- Header -->
    <section class="text-center py-12">
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-amber-400 mb-4">Spellcasting Guide</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            Learn the fundamentals of adding and utilizing spellcasting capabilities on your Pathfinder character.
        </p>
    </section>

    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16 space-y-12">

        <!-- Gameplay Basics -->
        <section class="bg-gray-800 rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-400 mb-4">Gameplay Basics</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
                Spells are magical abilities used by certain classes (Wizards, Sorcerers, Clerics, Druids, Bards, etc.). Not every class can cast spells; martials like Fighters and Rogues generally can't unless they take specific feats.
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-300 space-y-2">
                <li>Spells come in ranks 1–10. Higher-rank spells are more powerful. Your character can only cast spells up to the rank their class supports. For example,a 1st-level Wizard can only cast rank 1 spells (and cantrips).</li>
                <li>Most spellcasters use spell slots: a limited pool of "uses" per day, organized by rank. Casting a rank 2 spell uses one of your rank 2 slots. When you're out of slots, you can't cast those spells until you rest.</li>
                <li>Cantrips are rank 0 spells you can cast unlimited times. They automatically scale to your level. Every spellcaster gets them; use them when slots run out!</li>
            </ul>

            <!-- Video Placeholder -->
            <div class="mt-6 bg-gray-700 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
                <p class="text-gray-400">[ YouTube Video Placeholder: Gameplay Basics ]</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Traditions -->
        <section class="bg-gray-800 rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-400 mb-4">Traditions</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
                Spells belong to one of four magical traditions, which determines what you have access to. Each tradition represents a fundamentally different source and philosophy of magic, which shapes not just what spells you can cast, but the flavor and role of your character in the world.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Arcane (Magus, Wizard): The broadest and most versatile spell list in the game. It's rooted in intellectual mastery: the idea that magic is a science to be learned and controlled.
                    <ul>
                        <li>The widest variety of offensive spells (Fireball, Lightning Bolt, Disintegrate)</li>
                        <li>Powerful utility and battlefield control (Grease, Wall of Force, Dimension Door)</li>
                        <li>Very few healing spells, generally can't restore hit points</li>
                        <li>Limited access to nature or spirit-based magic</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>Divine (Champion, Cleric, Oracle): Divine magic flows from devotion, whether to a deity, a spiritual concept, or a cosmic force. It is the tradition most associated with healing and holy power, but it's far more than just a support tree.
                    <ul>
                        <li>The best healing spells in the game</li>
                        <li>Powerful buff and debuff magic</li>
                        <li>A mix of offensive, protective, and restorative spells</li>
                        <li>Note: Your deity's alignment and portfolio can restrict which spells you can access</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>Occult (Bard, Inquisitor, Psychic, Witch): The most unusual tradition, as it deals in the strange, the hidden, and the metaphysical. Where arcane magic is a science and divine magic is faith, occult magic is somewhere between art, intuition, and forbidden knowledge.
                    <ul>
                        <li>The best enchantment and illusion spells in the game</li>
                        <li>Powerful mental attacks and debuffs (Fear, Confusion, Phantasmal Killer)</li>
                        <li>Unique access to spirit and emotion-based magic</li>
                        <li>Limited healing and elemental blasting options</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>Primal (Druid, Ranger, Barbarian): Primal magic is the power of the natural world, harnessing fire, storms, animals, plants, and the cycle of life and death. It sits between arcane and divine in terms of healing ability, and has unmatched nature-flavored utility.
                    <ul>
                        <li>Strong elemental damage spells (Tempest Surge, Wildfire, Lightning Bolt)</li>
                        <li>Excellent summon spells, especially animals and nature creatures</li>
                        <li>Unique utility around terrain, plants, and animals (Speak with Animals, Tree Stride)</li>
                        <li>Fewer options for illusion, enchantment, and arcane-style utility</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ul>

            <!-- Traditions and Essences Video -->
            <iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/R3tNtwcEREg?si=FLPPa-Ms5k3kiG4W" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </section>

        <!-- Quick Tips -->
        <section class="bg-gray-800 rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-400 mb-4">Quick Tips</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-300 space-y-2">
                <li>Don’t min-max too early—balance matters</li>
                <li>Keep your gear updated regularly</li>
                <li>Read ability descriptions carefully</li>
                <li>Experiment with different builds</li>
            </ul>

            <!-- Video Placeholder -->
            <div class="mt-6 bg-gray-700 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
                <p class="text-gray-400">[ YouTube Video Placeholder: Tips & Tricks ]</p>
            </div>
        </section>

    </div>

</div>
